# Default owners — auto-requested as reviewers on every PR.
#
# @VerifyYou/dev-team reaches every engineer rather than one person:
#   - review-request delegation is OFF, so GitHub requests the whole team
#     (no round-robin) and every member is notified;
#   - a requested reviewer surfaces the PR in that member's Linear
#     "Needs your review" queue;
#   - GitHub never requests the PR author, so the author is excluded
#     automatically — and, unlike a single named owner, someone is still
#     requested when that person is the author.
#
# This is an auto-request mechanism, not an extra merge gate: the branch
# ruleset requires 1 approval and does NOT require a code-owner approval,
# so any one approval from a person with write access still clears merge.
#
# NOTE: a team is only a valid code owner if it is visible AND has write
# access to this repo — org base permission does not count, and an invalid
# entry is silently ignored. Both teams below were granted write on
# 2026-08-06. Do not remove those grants.
*                       @VerifyYou/dev-team

# Sensitive paths — @VerifyYou/code-admins is added alongside the team.
# Last matching pattern wins, so the team is repeated to keep it requested.
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @VerifyYou/dev-team @VerifyYou/code-admins
/.github/workflows/     @VerifyYou/dev-team @VerifyYou/code-admins
